  "basis_disclosure": "Every node is consumed on the U.S. Treasury CMT convention, the short end included. The published curve is a par yield curve and its yields are bond-equivalent yields for semi-annual-pay securities, so each node is read on a semi-annual compounding basis with ACT/ACT accrual approximated by exact half-year periods. Treatment follows from the tenor: nodes below six months carry no coupon before maturity and are pure discount instruments quoted coupon-equivalent, DF = (1 + y/2)^(-2t); the six-month node is a par bond with its single semi-annual coupon at maturity; nodes at one year and beyond are semi-annual coupon bonds priced at par, coupon = y / 2 with redemption at maturity. Forward rates surfaced from this curve are quoted on the same bond-equivalent semi-annual basis. The instrument `type` field (BILL_BEY below one year, CMT_PAR at one year and beyond) is descriptive metadata; the bootstrapper keys off the tenor alone. Below one month the zero curve holds the 1M node flat.",
